{"kind":"table","sheet":"Template","address":"A1:E37","rows":37,"cols":5,"values":[["It is recommended that you do not edit rubrics in spreadsheet format",null,null,null,null],["v1.0-s",null,null,null,null],["Name, class, and date",null,null,null,null],["Enter your complete name, class, and date in the final presentation.",null,null,null,null],[null,1,0,null,null],[null,"Complete","Incomplete",null,null],[null,"1 pt = complete name, class, and date.","0 pts = name, class, or date is missing or incomplete.",null,null],["Four-slide structure, title, and student name",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: (1) uses a Canva presentation; (2) includes at least four slides; (3) Slide 1 has a clear title about ultrasonic sensors; and (4) Slide 1 includes the student's full name.",null,null,null,null],[null,7,5,3,0],[null,"Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Below Standard","Unacceptable"],[null,"7 pts = 4 checks.","5 pts = 2–3.","3 pts = 1.","0 pts = 0 or no presentation."],["What is an ultrasonic sensor?",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: explains that an ultrasonic sensor (1) measures distance; (2) sends a high-frequency sound pulse; (3) listens for the returning echo; and (4) uses the echo's travel time to determine distance.",null,null,null,null],[null,7,5,3,0],[null,"Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Below Standard","Unacceptable"],[null,"7 pts = 4 checks.","5 pts = 2–3.","3 pts = 1.","0 pts = 0 or no explanation."],["Parts of the ultrasonic sensor",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: correctly identifies and explains (1) VCC/power; (2) GND/ground; (3) TRIG and the transmitting element that sends the pulse; and (4) ECHO and the receiving element that detects the return. Labels or a clear diagram may be used.",null,null,null,null],[null,7,5,3,0],[null,"Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Below Standard","Unacceptable"],[null,"7 pts = 4 checks.","5 pts = 2–3.","3 pts = 1.","0 pts = 0 or no parts identified."],["Sensor connection and data collection",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: using the teacher-provided code, the student (1) connects VCC and GND correctly; (2) connects TRIG and ECHO to the assigned pins; (3) keeps the circuit safe, powered correctly, and organized; and (4) obtains stable readings at different object distances. Writing the code is not assessed.",null,null,null,null],[null,7,5,3,0],[null,"Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Below Standard","Unacceptable"],[null,"7 pts = 4 checks.","5 pts = 2–3.","3 pts = 1.","0 pts = 0 or no working setup."],["Five distance readings and a reliable near/far threshold",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: Slide 4 (1) records at least 5 actual distance readings; (2) gives the unit for every reading; (3) states one numerical threshold and clearly defines which values are Near and which are Far; and (4) uses the collected readings or repeated tests to explain why the threshold is reliable.",null,null,null,null],[null,7,5,3,0],[null,"Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Below Standard","Unacceptable"],[null,"7 pts = 4 checks.","5 pts = 2–3.","3 pts = 1.","0 pts = 0 or no readings/threshold."],["Punctuality, readiness, and respect",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: (1) Submits all required work by the deadline; (2) arrives with a charged computer, charger, login access, pen, and notebook; (3) handles the computer, charger, sensor, cables, and workspace carefully; and (4) begins on time, follows directions, and does not interfere with another student’s device or work.",null,null,null,null],[null,4,3,1,0],[null,"Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Below Standard","Unacceptable"],[null,"4 pts = 4 steps.","3 pts = 2–3.","1 pt = 1.","0 pts = none."]]}
